0..79 Comment "// A record type\'s faces: each a set of the record\'s labels, named in a `where`"
80..158 Comment "// block after the type. A static bracket after the type fixes some fields, by"
159..179 Comment "// label or by face."
180..182 Comment "//"
183..259 Comment "// A record type\'s labels are its boundary. A face over them names a part of"
260..334 Comment "// the record, so a later form restricts a value to that part. The checker"
335..413 Comment "// checks each fixed value at its field\'s type. A value of the patched type is"
414..493 Comment "// the record of the fields the bracket leaves free. A name at it reads a fixed"
494..534 Comment "// field as the value the bracket fixes."
535..537 Comment "//"
538..615 Comment "// The block names each face as a theory\'s `face` member does. The block ends"
616..695 Comment "// the type member at its `}`, as a `data` block ends its declaration. A record"
696..764 Comment "// type with no block keeps its labels as its boundary all the same."
765..833 Comment "// `Config[.port = 443, .tls = true]` fixes two fields by label, and"
834..910 Comment "// `Config[secure ↦ *{.port = 443, .tls = true}]` fixes the face `secure`."
911..942 Comment "// `|->` spells `↦` in ASCII."
943..945 Comment "//"
946..1024 Comment "// - see: `pathological/desc/record-faces.gandr` — a face past the labels, a"
1025..1102 Comment "//   face named twice, and a bracket naming a field or a face the type lacks,"
1103..1115 Comment "//   refused"
1116..1195 Comment "// - see: `model/desc/shaped-signature.gandr` — a theory\'s `boundary` and its"
1196..1206 Comment "//   faces"
1207..1269 Comment "// - owes: #5578 — a configuration coerced to a patched type"
1270..1339 Comment "// - owes: #5579 — an element of a patched type coerced back to the"
1340..1358 Comment "//   configuration"
1359..1439 Comment "// - owes: #5106 — two faces fixed at once, whose values agree where the faces"
1440..1449 Comment "//   meet"
1451..1528 Comment "/// A server\'s configuration: the faces `secure` and `addr` meet at the port."
